# Keep this file at the repo root. Prettier does not discover .prettierignore
# hierarchically the way it discovers config files: it reads exactly one, from the
# working directory (or --ignore-path / the editor's prettier.ignorePath). A copy
# inside tailored-resumes-feature/ is silently ignored, and the resumes get mangled.
#
# Resume Markdown is parsed back into a PDF by
# tailored-resumes-feature/scripts/render_resume.py, which expects *Role | Dates*
# subtitles. Prettier rewrites `*em*` to `_em_` (not configurable) and escapes bare
# `*`, so formatting these files breaks the PDF layout without any error. Job
# descriptions are model input and should reach the prompt exactly as pasted.
tailored-resumes-feature/tailored-resumes/
tailored-resumes-feature/job-descriptions/
